From: Droidloom <droidloom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wm: include routed touch in Droidloom display configuration

Denial owns physical input devices. Droidloom's bridge delivers touchscreen
MotionEvents directly to each task, so enumerating Android input nodes alone
incorrectly selects notouch resources and advertises no touch to app stores.
Require both the Droidloom task marker and the product's touchscreen feature;
ordinary Android products retain their input-device-derived configuration.

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.java
@@ -2918,6 +2918,13 @@
 
         // Update the configuration based on available input devices, lid switch,
         // and platform configuration.
-        config.touchscreen = Configuration.TOUCHSCREEN_NOTOUCH;
+        // Droidloom receives touch through its task-token bridge, without
+        // exposing Denial's physical input nodes as Android input devices.
+        // Include that routed source only when the product declares it.
+        final boolean hasDroidloomTouch = mWmService.mIsTouchDevice
+                && android.os.SystemProperties.getBoolean(
+                        "ro.vendor.droidloom.surfaceflinger_tasks", false);
+        config.touchscreen = hasDroidloomTouch
+                ? Configuration.TOUCHSCREEN_FINGER : Configuration.TOUCHSCREEN_NOTOUCH;
         config.keyboard = Configuration.KEYBOARD_NOKEYS;
         config.navigation = Configuration.NAVIGATION_NONAV;
